<x_1999:xhtmldiv>
  <x_1999:xhtmltable>
    <x_1999:xhtmltr>
      <x_1999:xhtmlth rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Range:</x_1999:xhtmlth>
      <x_1999:xhtmltd rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Literal</x_1999:xhtmltd>
    </x_1999:xhtmltr>
  </x_1999:xhtmltable>
  <x_1999:xhtmlp>
    <x_1999:xhtmlcode>
      <x_1999:xhtmla rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">foaf:Person</x_1999:xhtmla>
    </x_1999:xhtmlcode>
  </x_1999:xhtmlp>
  <x_1999:xhtmlp>
    <x_1999:xhtmlcode>
      <x_1999:xhtmla rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">foaf:weblog</x_1999:xhtmla>
    </x_1999:xhtmlcode>
  </x_1999:xhtmlp>
  <x_1999:xhtmlp>
    <x_1999:xhtmlcode>
      <x_1999:xhtmla rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">foaf:myersBriggs</x_1999:xhtmla>
    </x_1999:xhtmlcode>
  </x_1999:xhtmlp>
  <x_1999:xhtmlp>
    <x_1999:xhtmla/>
  </x_1999:xhtmlp>
  <x_1999:xhtmlp>
    <x_1999:xhtmla/>
  </x_1999:xhtmlp>
  <x_1999:xhtmlp>
    <x_1999:xhtmla/>
  </x_1999:xhtmlp>
  <x_1999:xhtmlh3 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Property: foaf:myersBriggs</x_1999:xhtmlh3>
  <x_1999:xhtmlem rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">myersBriggs</x_1999:xhtmlem>
  <x_1999:xhtmlbr rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"></x_1999:xhtmlbr>
  <x_1999:xhtmlp rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">
This FOAF property suggests some interesting uses, some of which could perhaps be used to 
test the claims made by proponents of the MBTI (eg. an analysis of weblog postings 
filtered by MBTI type). However it should be noted that MBTI FOAF descriptions are 
self-selecting; MBTI categories may not be uniformly appealing to the people they 
describe. Further, there is probably a degree of cultural specificity implicit in the 
assumptions made by many questionaire-based MBTI tools; the MBTI system may not make 
sense in cultural settings beyond those it was created for. 
</x_1999:xhtmlp>
  <x_1999:xhtmlp rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">
Note: Myers Briggs Type Indicator and MBTI are registered trademarks of Consulting 
Psychologists Press Inc. Oxford Psycholgists Press Ltd has exclusive rights to the 
trademark in the UK. 
</x_1999:xhtmlp>
</x_1999:xhtmldiv>

